  "limitations": "Spherical (Web) Mercator tiling only, latitude limited to plus/minus 85.05 degrees, zoom 0-28. Tiles are named, not downloaded; there are no tile URLs, imagery or network access. Tile x/y must be below 2^z. Parent and siblings are refused for zoom 0. bbox_to_tile returns the single smallest tile containing the whole box, which can be much larger than the box.",
  "port_notes": "Ports tileToBBOX, tileToGeoJSON, tile2lon, tile2lat, pointToTile, pointToTileFraction, getChildren, getParent, getSiblings, tileToQuadkey, quadkeyToTile, bboxToTile and getBboxZoom from index.js at v1.0.1, reproducing JavaScript 32-bit integer semantics of & and >>> in bboxToTile. getParent quirk (!tile[1]%2) is equivalent to integer halving for valid non-negative tiles. hasTile/hasSiblings/tilesEqual are not exposed.",
